<title>UK: Transco UK gas forecasts for May 21.</title>
<headline>Transco UK gas forecasts for May 21.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Transco, the pipeline and transport arm of BG plc, has announced the following forecasts and data for UK gas consumption in the period May 19 to 21.</p>
<p>DEMAND:</p>
<p>(mcm = million cubic metres)</p>
<p>May 19 (actual) 161 mcm, 37 percent of peak day demand</p>
<p>May 20 (forecast) 168 mcm, 39 percent of peak day demand</p>
<p>May 21 (forecast) 180 mcm, 42 percent of peak day demand</p>
<p>TEMPERATURE:</p>
<p>(SNT = seasonal normal temperature)</p>
<p>May 19 (actual) 14.0 Celsius, SNT 13.3 Celsius</p>
<p>May 20 (forecast) 13.1 Celsius, SNT 13.4 Celsius</p>
<p>May 21 (forecast) 11.4 Celsius, SNT 13.5 Celsius</p>
<p>There was no supply interruption called for Tuesday, with none expected for Wednesday.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom, +44 171 542 6412</p>
</text>
